                                    <h1>Legal Tech &amp; Lawyer SaaS Development Guide 2026</h1>
                                    <p>Legal tech is finally having its long-predicted moment — LLMs made contract review, drafting, and e-discovery genuinely useful. Modern legal tech platforms combine case management + document AI + collaboration in ways that materially change lawyer productivity. Here is what to build and buy.</p>
                                    <h2>The Legal Tech Landscape</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Case management (law firms):</strong> Clio, MyCase, PracticePanther (SMB); Litify, Elite 3E (enterprise).<br><strong>Contract lifecycle management (CLM):</strong> DocuSign CLM, Icertis, Ironclad, Agiloft.<br><strong>AI contract review:</strong> Harvey, Spellbook, Klarity, custom.<br><strong>E-discovery:</strong> Relativity, Everlaw, Logikcull.<br><strong>Legal research:</strong> Westlaw, LexisNexis, Casetext (Thomson Reuters), Manupatra (India).<br><strong>Legal ops:</strong> Simple Legal, Priori (spend + matter management).</p>
                                    <h2>Where AI Actually Wins in Legal</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Contract review + redlining:</strong> LLM-based first-pass review saves 40-70% of associate time.<br><strong>Drafting standard documents:</strong> NDAs, employment agreements, MSAs — 60-80% draft time reduction.<br><strong>Legal research summarisation:</strong> 3-5x faster case-law review.<br><strong>Discovery review:</strong> AI-assisted document classification and privilege review.<br><strong>Deposition prep:</strong> transcript analysis + issue spotting.</p>
                                    <h2>Regional Notes</h2>
                                    <p><strong>India:</strong> Case-management software adoption growing (SpotDraft, EquiCorp Analytics). Manupatra + SCC Online for research. Bar Council compliance considerations.<br><strong>UAE:</strong> Legal 500 firms adopting global tools. DIFC + ADGM specialty needs.<br><strong>USA:</strong> Most mature market. AI tools (Harvey especially) reshaping BigLaw.<br><strong>UK:</strong> Magic Circle firms leading AI adoption. LawGeex / Kira legacy.<br><strong>Australia:</strong> LawVu, ClioAU growing.</p>
                                    <h2>Cost + Timeline</h2>
                                    <p><strong>MVP legal tech SaaS (16-24 weeks):</strong> ₹40-90 lakh / $48K-108K.<br><strong>Full CLM or case management (24-40 weeks):</strong> ₹1-3 Cr / $120K-360K.<br><strong>Enterprise legal ops platform (36-56 weeks):</strong> ₹3-8 Cr / $360K-960K.</p>
                                    <h2>Compliance Requirements</h2>
                                    <p>Attorney-client privilege must be preserved — LLM providers with data retention policies matter. On-prem or VPC deployment often required for BigLaw. SOC 2 Type II mandatory for enterprise sales. Trust matters more than any feature.</p>

